{"ts": "2026-08-31T22:39:15Z", "task_id": "TASK-7001", "attempt": 1, "verdict": "CHANGES_REQUESTED", "failed_tests": 9, "real_execution": true, "applied_files": 4, "feedback": [{"file": "src/config.py", "line": 57, "issue": "@lru_cache(maxsize=1) on get_settings() freezes the first-call snapshot for the process lifetime, so monkeypatched env vars in later tests are ignored. This is the root cause of the failures in test_env_var_overrides, the 4 falsy test_paper_only_boolean_parsing cases, and test_get_settings_fresh_each_call (confirmed by the failure pattern FFF....FFFF..F.F..), and it also means config could never be refreshed at runtime.", "remediation": "Remove the lru_cache decorator and compute settings fresh on each call (the plan explicitly permits this), or keep the cache and add an autouse fixture in tests/conftest.py that calls get_settings.cache_clear() before every test."}, {"file": "tests/test_config.py", "line": 28, "issue": "test_default_settings asserts settings.alpaca_base_url == '', but the implementation defaults alpaca_base_url to DEFAULT_ALPACA_BASE_URL ('https://paper-api.alpaca.markets'). The test contradicts the shipped code, so this test can never pass.", "remediation": "Change the assertion to compare against the intended default, e.g. 'assert settings.alpaca_base_url == DEFAULT_ALPACA_BASE_URL' after importing DEFAULT_ALPACA_BASE_URL from src.config (a paper-API URL default is sane and consistent with paper_only=True)."}, {"file": "tests/test_config.py", "line": 59, "issue": "test_watchlist_parsing_edge_cases expects WATCHLIST='' and WATCHLIST='   ' to yield an empty tuple, which contradicts both _parse_watchlist (falls back to DEFAULT_WATCHLIST) and the plan's edge case that an empty WATCHLIST must fall back to the default 10-ticker watchlist. Fails even once caching is fixed.", "remediation": "Update the expectations for '' and '   ' to DEFAULT_WATCHLIST so the test matches the specified fall-back behavior."}]}
