{"ts": "2026-09-01T23:09:56Z", "task_id": "TASK-7003B", "attempt": 3, "verdict": "CHANGES_REQUESTED", "failed_tests": 2, "real_execution": true, "applied_files": 1, "feedback": [{"file": "src/data/market_data.py", "line": 148, "issue": "Acceptance gate not met: the task's pre-seeded tests tests/test_market_data.py::test_cache_hit_skips_second_download and ::test_cache_miss_for_different_ticker fail with TypeError. The miss-path store cache.set(cache_key, _to_json_safe_payload(frame)) is the prime suspect: per the Cache contract, Cache.set raises TypeError when json.dumps cannot encode the value, meaning the coercion in _json_safe_value does not cover every value/key shape the fixtures exercise (likely offenders not handled: non-string dict keys such as tuples produced by reset_index().to_dict(orient='list') for MultiIndex columns, pd.NaT, pd.Timedelta).", "remediation": "Run `pytest tests/test_market_data.py::test_cache_hit_skips_second_download -x -q` and read the full traceback to identify the exact non-serializable object; extend the payload conversion (stringify non-str dict keys, handle NaT/Timedelta/datetime64 variants) so cache.set always receives a plain dict of lists of JSON-native scalars, while preserving the specified reset_index-based storage shape."}, {"file": "src/data/market_data.py", "line": 138, "issue": "The cache-hit path can also surface the TypeError on the second fetch: _rebuild_frame (pd.DataFrame(stored) plus pd.to_datetime on the stored index column) must tolerate exactly what was stored and restore the DatetimeIndex; its correctness is currently unverifiable because the store/round-trip fails first, leaving the acceptance criterion 'cache hit avoids second _download call' unverified.", "remediation": "After fixing the stored payload, verify the full round trip end-to-end with a real Cache over tmp_path: the second fetch must not invoke _download again and the rebuilt frame must equal the first (same columns, values, and DatetimeIndex); then re-run tests/test_market_data.py and tests/test_cache.py until fully green."}]}
