{"ts": "2026-09-04T00:45:22Z", "task_id": "TASK-7007B", "attempt": 1, "verdict": "CHANGES_REQUESTED", "failed_tests": 3, "real_execution": true, "applied_files": 1, "feedback": [{"file": "src/agents/risk_manager.py", "line": 248, "issue": "Acceptance criterion 'tests/test_risk_manager.py fully green' is not met: the three failures (test_vetoes_missing_report_citations, test_vetoes_missing_debate_citations, test_missing_citation_check_bea...) are all rule-1 citation-gate assertion failures. The 'missing citations: <agent/name>' strings built via the _display_name heuristic (probing agent/name/agent_name/analyst/... and falling back to the mapping key or 'debate') do not match the exact identifiers the pre-seeded tests expect.", "remediation": "Read tests/test_risk_manager.py and pin the exact name source and message format the tests assert (e.g., reports mapping key vs. a specific AnalystReport/DebateRecord field, and the expected debate identifier); replace the attribute-guessing _display_name with that fixed source and emit the exact expected strings for both the report and debate cases."}, {"file": "src/agents/risk_manager.py", "line": 50, "issue": "TASK-7007A types are resolved by importlib-probing ~24 guessed module paths, which can silently bind wrong/incompatible AnalystReport/DebateRecord/RiskDecision definitions and leads to the defensive alias machinery below.", "remediation": "Use search.code_search for 'class AnalystReport'/'class RiskDecision' to find the concrete TASK-7007A module, import the three types directly from it, and delete the candidate-module list and _load_types fallback."}, {"file": "src/agents/risk_manager.py", "line": 168, "issue": "_build_decision guesses RiskDecision field names via an alias table (symbol/is_approved/reasons/veto_reason/override/...) with positional fallbacks, which can populate wrong or missing fields on the real dataclass and obscures the actual mismatch.", "remediation": "Construct RiskDecision with exactly the fields defined in TASK-7007A once the module is located; remove the alias dict and positional fallbacks."}]}
