{"ts": "2026-09-04T12:00:49Z", "task_id": "TASK-7011", "attempt": 3, "verdict": "CHANGES_REQUESTED", "failed_tests": 4, "real_execution": true, "applied_files": 2, "feedback": [{"file": "src/config.py", "line": 1, "issue": "The diff rewrites the entire pre-existing src/config.py (hunk base is /dev/null) instead of making the required additive change. The rewrite replaced the original Settings surface that tests/test_config.py pins, causing AttributeError regressions in test_default_settings and test_paper_only_env_var_parsing (4 failures total, up from a fully green baseline).", "remediation": "Restore the baseline src/config.py verbatim and apply ONLY the additive module-level reset_settings_cache() hook. Keep the original Settings class, DEFAULT_WATCHLIST, DEFAULT_TIER_MODEL_MAP, SETTINGS, and fresh-per-call get_settings() exactly as they were; do not re-derive field defaults or helper behavior."}, {"file": "src/config.py", "line": 95, "issue": "Reimplemented Settings uses dataclass default_factory helpers (e.g. _env_watchlist with WATCHLIST env name, _env_bool with 1/true/yes/on parsing) that differ from the original implementation exercised by tests/test_config.py, so constructor kwargs and parsed values no longer match what the tests expect.", "remediation": "Reuse the original Settings field definitions and env-parsing behavior from the baseline file so test_default_settings and test_paper_only_env_var_parsing pass unchanged; add reset_settings_cache() below get_settings() as a safe no-op that never caches."}, {"file": "src/cli.py", "line": 48, "issue": "Broad 'except Exception' fallbacks silently substitute a stub run_pipeline and an _EmptyDecisionStore when imports fail, which masks real wiring errors (this task previously failed with ERR_CLI_WIRING) and can make scan/decisions print nothing while appearing to succeed.", "remediation": "Import run_pipeline from src.pipeline.graph and DecisionStore unconditionally so a broken dependency fails loudly; remove or drastically narrow the try/except fallbacks so missing modules surface as errors instead of empty output."}]}
