{"ts": "2026-09-04T12:36:59Z", "task_id": "TASK-7011", "attempt": 3, "verdict": "CHANGES_REQUESTED", "failed_tests": 4, "real_execution": true, "applied_files": 2, "feedback": [{"file": "src/cli.py", "line": 186, "issue": "tests/test_cli.py::test_scan_prints_decision_rows fails: scan prints decisions as space-separated 'ticker signal confidence approved' lines, but the pre-seeded test expects the pinned format from tests/test_cli.py (e.g., 'AAPL BUY 0.87 approved=True' style). Since the test monkeypatches src.cli.run_pipeline and the pipeline is importable in this repo, the guarded import/fallback machinery is unnecessary complexity; the real problem is the output format not matching the test's assertion.", "remediation": "Read tests/test_cli.py::test_scan_prints_decision_rows and replicate its exact expected line format verbatim in _decision_line/scan output (one line per decision containing ticker, signal, confidence, approved in the order and style the test asserts). Remove the try/except fallback import and make the plain module-level re-export 'from src.pipeline.graph import run_pipeline' the only path."}, {"file": "src/config.py", "line": 1, "issue": "The diff replaces the entire pre-existing src/config.py (shown as --- /dev/null) instead of making an additive change. This regressed tests/test_config.py (test_default_settings and at least one other config test failed; baseline was green). The rewritten defaults/env parsing (e.g., empty-string watchlist falling back to DEFAULT_WATCHLIST, alpaca_base_url default, _parse_bool semantics, Settings field set) no longer match the behavior the existing tests pin.", "remediation": "Restore the original src/config.py content and apply only the requested addition: def reset_settings_cache() -> None as a no-op-style compatibility hook that clears any module-level cache (without introducing caching in get_settings(), which must keep constructing a fresh Settings() per call). Keep the original DEFAULT_WATCHLIST, DEFAULT_TIER_MODEL_MAP, Settings fields/defaults, get_settings() body, and SETTINGS exactly as they were."}, {"file": "src/config.py", "line": 96, "issue": "reset_settings_cache() mutates the module-level SETTINGS global by reassigning it to a fresh get_settings(). The task specifies a hook that 'clears any module-level settings cache so the next get_settings() re-reads the environment' — with fresh-per-call get_settings() there is nothing to clear, and reassigning SETTINGS changes observable module state that existing tests may pin (this is part of the test_config.py regression).", "remediation": "Make reset_settings_cache() a pure compatibility hook: if (and only if) the original file had no cache, either leave SETTINGS untouched or restore whatever cache-clearing behavior the original module had. Do not introduce new side effects beyond clearing a hypothetical cache."}]}
