{"ts": "2026-09-04T18:54:00Z", "task_id": "TASK-7011B", "attempt": 1, "verdict": "CHANGES_REQUESTED", "failed_tests": 2, "real_execution": true, "applied_files": 1, "feedback": [{"file": "src/cli.py", "line": 140, "issue": "REAL TEST FAILURE: tests/test_cli.py::test_scan_prints_decision_rows fails (exit code 1, no FAKE1/HOLD in stdout). Root cause: the test monkeypatches src.cli.run_pipeline with a plain function that returns the decision list synchronously, but scan wraps the call in asyncio.run(...). asyncio.run requires an awaitable and raises 'ValueError: a coroutine was expected', so scan crashes. The task spec mandates calling the module-level run_pipeline inside the body (so the monkeypatch applies), not necessarily via asyncio.run; the safe pattern is: result = run_pipeline(ticker_list, _components()); if inspect.iscoroutine(result): result = asyncio.run(result) -- or have _components/the pipeline path handle async explicitly. The same bug affects the paper-run command body.", "remediation": "Call the module-level run_pipeline directly inside the scan/paper-run bodies without forcing asyncio.run around it; only await/asyncio.run when the returned value is actually a coroutine, so the monkeypatched sync stub works and the real async pipeline still runs."}, {"file": "src/cli.py", "line": 45, "issue": "REAL TEST FAILURE: tests/test_cli.py::test_app_has_expected_commands fails. The spec requires a module-level 'def _store() -> DecisionStore' constructing the project DecisionStore with db_path=Path(os.environ.get('DECISIONS_DB', 'data/decisions.sqlite3')). This diff instead adds a dynamic __import__ loop (_resolve_decision_store_class) plus a private sqlite fallback (_FallbackDecisionStore), which deviates from the mandated seam and can import unexpected modules during collection/invocation, changing app behavior vs. what the tests expect.", "remediation": "Remove _FallbackDecisionStore and the module-probing loop; import the project's DecisionStore directly (plain top-level import from its actual project location) and implement _store() as: return DecisionStore(db_path=Path(os.environ.get('DECISIONS_DB', 'data/decisions.sqlite3'))). Keep the call inside command bodies so cli._store stays monkeypatchable."}, {"file": "src/cli.py", "line": 3, "issue": "The file adds imports and machinery (json, sqlite3, dynamic imports) beyond the specified scope; the plan forbids try/except fallback import patterns around seams and extra I/O outside the _store/_components seams. This is secondary to the two test failures but should be cleaned up in the same pass.", "remediation": "Strip to the minimal required surface: module-level imports (os, asyncio if still needed, Path, typer, get_settings, run_pipeline, DecisionStore), app = typer.Typer(), _components() (non-raising, minimal wiring), _store(), and the four commands scan/paper-run/decisions/show-config."}]}
