{"ts": "2026-09-04T19:24:09Z", "task_id": "TASK-7012", "attempt": 2, "verdict": "CHANGES_REQUESTED", "failed_tests": 3, "real_execution": true, "applied_files": 1, "feedback": [{"file": "src/pipeline/smoke.py", "line": 67, "issue": "KeyError: 'pipeline_runner' — the injected components dict used by tests/test_smoke.py does not contain the 'pipeline_runner' key, so all three new tests fail. The implementation invented a component key instead of mirroring the graph contracts from TASK-7011B that the suite stubs.", "remediation": "Inspect tests/test_smoke.py and the TASK-7011B graph contract to learn the exact component keys the stubs provide (e.g., 'graph' rather than 'pipeline_runner'), then access components with those exact keys (components[...].run / broker_submit) so injected stubs work as-is."}, {"file": "src/pipeline/smoke.py", "line": 74, "issue": "Broker invocation assumes components['broker'].broker_submit(decision.orders) with an .orders attribute on the decision; this must match the stubbed component contract or additional failures will remain after the key fix.", "remediation": "Mirror the exact decision/order shape and broker key used by the test stubs (attribute vs dict access, broker_submit signature/return) so orders_submitted reflects len(broker_submit(...)) and is 0 for the dry-run [] return."}, {"file": "src/pipeline/smoke.py", "line": 130, "issue": "Silent ImportError fallback to _FallbackDecisionStore masks a missing/broken DecisionStore import; the dry-run acceptance test ('dry_run submits nothing and writes the decision log') could pass while nothing was persisted to the DECISIONS_DB SQLite file.", "remediation": "Remove the fallback and always use the real DecisionStore from TASK-7011B (src/decisions/store.py or its actual location), constructing it at the DECISIONS_DB env path (default 'data/decisions.sqlite3') with parent-dir creation, so the decision row is genuinely written and testable."}]}
