{"ts": "2026-09-04T20:04:27Z", "task_id": "TASK-7012", "attempt": 1, "verdict": "CHANGES_REQUESTED", "failed_tests": 2, "real_execution": true, "applied_files": 1, "feedback": [{"file": "src/pipeline/smoke.py", "line": 121, "issue": "build_order_plan is invoked with 7 positional arguments (tk, reports, debate, quant, veto, account, day_trade_dates), but the pinned test stub accepts only 4-5 positional args, raising 'TypeError: _stub_components.<locals>.<lambda>() takes from 4 to 5 positional arguments but 7 were given'. Both failing tests trace to this line, aborting the per-ticker flow before the decision log write, so 'tests fully green' is not satisfied.", "remediation": "Align the build_order_plan invocation with the exact stub signature in tests/test_smoke.py (the contract only requires that components['account'] and components['day_trade_dates'] are used). Reduce the call to the arguments the stub actually accepts, e.g. components['build_order_plan'](tk, quant, veto, account, day_trade_dates) or whichever arity/order the test's lambda defines, and make _build_real_components' planner conform to the same call shape."}]}
{"ts": "2026-09-04T20:12:59Z", "task_id": "TASK-7012", "attempt": 2, "verdict": "CHANGES_REQUESTED", "failed_tests": 2, "real_execution": true, "applied_files": 1, "feedback": [{"file": "src/pipeline/smoke.py", "line": 117, "issue": "store.log_decision() is called with keyword argument 'symbol', but DecisionStore.log_decision() does not accept it -> TypeError: unexpected keyword argument 'symbol' on every ticker in every run. This breaks the required decision logging in both dry-run and live modes and is the direct cause of both failing tests (including test_dry_run_writes_decision_log).", "remediation": "Inspect the actual signature of DecisionStore.log_decision in src/store/decisions.py and call it with exactly the parameter names it defines (e.g., ticker/symbol field name and its expected payload/argument shape). Keep the per-run DecisionStore(db_path=Path(os.environ.get('DECISIONS_DB', 'data/decisions.sqlite3'))) construction and per-ticker logging, then re-run tests/test_smoke.py to full green."}, {"file": "README.md", "line": 1, "issue": "The task objective requires documenting the manual live paper run in README; the diff documents it only in the smoke.py module docstring, and README.md was not touched.", "remediation": "Add a short 'Manual live paper run' section to README.md covering ALPACA_API_KEY/ALPACA_SECRET_KEY env vars, DECISIONS_DB, and an asyncio.run(run_smoke([...], dry_run=False)) example."}]}
