{"ts": "2026-09-04T23:02:42Z", "task_id": "TASK-7013", "attempt": 3, "verdict": "CHANGES_REQUESTED", "failed_tests": 6, "real_execution": true, "applied_files": 2, "feedback": [{"file": "src/cli.py", "line": 196, "issue": "_run_and_print unconditionally wraps the pipeline call in asyncio.run(...). tests/test_wiring.py (line 263) monkeypatches src.cli.run_pipeline with a synchronous stub returning a plain list of decisions, so asyncio.run raises ValueError('a coroutine was expected, got [{...}]'), the command exits 1 instead of 0, and the decision-audit assertions downstream of the command also fail. This root cause accounts for the CLI-delegation failures among the 6 failing tests.", "remediation": "Bridge sync/async results: capture `result = run_pipeline(tickers, _components(submit=submit))` and then `decisions = asyncio.run(result) if inspect.isawaitable(result) else result` (add `import inspect` at module top). This keeps the real async src.pipeline.graph.run_pipeline working while satisfying the sync-stub contract exercised by test_wiring.py."}, {"file": "src/cli.py", "line": 198, "issue": "`store = _store()` runs outside any error guard; if DecisionStore construction raises (e.g., missing/unwritable DB directory), the entire scan/paper-run command aborts before any decision is printed, violating the spec requirement that any store failure print one warning line and never abort the command.", "remediation": "Guard store construction (fall back to None and skip persistence with a single warning) or move construction inside the per-decision try/except block so persistence failures degrade to warnings."}]}
