{"ts": "2026-09-04T23:11:59Z", "task_id": "TASK-7013", "attempt": 1, "verdict": "CHANGES_REQUESTED", "failed_tests": 7, "real_execution": true, "applied_files": 2, "feedback": [{"file": "src/cli.py", "line": 148, "issue": "Real test run: 7 failures, all showing 'AttributeError: <module src.cli> has no attribute _store' (tests/test_wiring.py:259). _run_and_print constructs a local DecisionStore inside the function, but the pre-seeded wiring tests monkeypatch/expect a module-level src.cli._store attribute for the decision-audit seam; the local construction makes that attribute nonexistent and the mocked store is never called.", "remediation": "Expose the store at module level in src/cli.py (e.g. try: _store = DecisionStore(db_path=os.environ.get('DECISIONS_DB', 'data/decisions.sqlite3')) except Exception: _store = None) and have _run_and_print resolve the store via the module attribute at call time (so monkeypatching src.cli._store takes effect); keep the single-warning, never-abort try/except around store.log_decision(_jsonable(decision))."}, {"file": "src/cli.py", "line": 148, "issue": "The CLI audit path hardcodes db_path='data/decisions.sqlite3' and ignores the DECISIONS_DB env var, diverging from the smoke path which honors DECISIONS_DB; tests that redirect the decision DB via the env var will not observe CLI-logged decisions.", "remediation": "Read the same DECISIONS_DB environment variable (default 'data/decisions.sqlite3') when constructing the module-level store so both CLI and smoke audit paths write to the same configurable location."}, {"file": "src/cli.py", "line": 172, "issue": "The 'decisions' command also builds its own DecisionStore(db_path='data/decisions.sqlite3') instead of reading through the module-level store, so it will not reflect a monkeypatched or env-redirected store used by the audit path.", "remediation": "Use the module-level _store (or a helper resolving DECISIONS_DB) in the decisions command so reads and writes share one seam."}]}
{"ts": "2026-09-04T23:19:00Z", "task_id": "TASK-7013", "attempt": 2, "verdict": "CHANGES_REQUESTED", "failed_tests": 9, "real_execution": true, "applied_files": 2, "feedback": [{"file": "src/cli.py", "line": 106, "issue": "Corrupted dict key in the primary _components return: '极news' instead of 'fetch_news'. The component contract requires all 12 keys including 'fetch_news'; tests asserting the exact key set (tests/test_wiring.py) fail because the key is missing/misspelled.", "remediation": "Replace '极news' with 'fetch_news' in the primary return dict."}, {"file": "src/cli.py", "line": 135, "issue": "Corrupted dict key in the fallback _components return: 'generate_s极nal' instead of 'generate_signal'. The fallback dict is missing the required 'generate_signal' key, so any test exercising the never-raise fallback path (key-set and identity assertions) fails.", "remediation": "Replace 'generate_s极nal' with 'generate_signal' in the fallback return dict."}, {"file": "src/cli.py", "line": 24, "issue": "DecisionStore is constructed once at module import time into _store. Tests that set DECISIONS_DB (or monkeypatch src.cli.DecisionStore) after import never see it, so decision-logging tests fail; additionally, when construction fails and _store is None, decisions are silently dropped with no warning line at all.", "remediation": "Build the store lazily at call time inside _run_and_print using os.environ.get('DECISIONS_DB', 'data/decisions.sqlite3'), wrapped in try/except that prints exactly one warning line on failure and never aborts the command."}]}
{"ts": "2026-09-04T23:27:01Z", "task_id": "TASK-7013", "attempt": 3, "verdict": "CHANGES_REQUESTED", "failed_tests": 2, "real_execution": true, "applied_files": 2, "feedback": [{"file": "src/pipeline/smoke.py", "line": 48, "issue": "The real test run still shows 2 failures, and the error tail pinpoints ValueError at asyncio/runners.py: 'a coroutine was expected, got {'client': <LLMClient...>, 'fetch_ohlcv': <function _components.<locals>.fetch_ohlcv_closure ...>}' -- i.e. asyncio.run was handed the components dict produced by _build_real_components. Since _run_and_print's isawaitable guard in cli.py is correct, the pinned test must be invoking _build_real_components through asyncio.run (the pre-existing pinned coroutine contract this task explicitly says was regressed). The diff's plain 'def _build_real_components' breaks that contract.", "remediation": "Restore the pinned async shape while keeping exactly one effective line in the body: 'async def _build_real_components(dry_run: bool) -> Dict[str, Any]: return dict(build_cli_components(submit=not dry_run))'. Then inside run_smoke use 'components = await _build_real_components(dry_run)' on the components-is-None branch (line 67), or call build_cli_components(submit=not dry_run) directly per Part C. Verify against the exact failing test body in tests/test_smoke.py / tests/test_wiring.py."}, {"file": "src/pipeline/smoke.py", "line": 83, "issue": "run_smoke unconditionally awaits run_pipeline(list(tickers), copy). If any pinned test monkeypatches src.pipeline.smoke.run_pipeline with a sync callable returning a plain list (the same monkeypatch shape mechanism (1) documents for src.cli), 'await' on a list raises TypeError -- a likely candidate for the second failure.", "remediation": "Mirror the CLI's pinned result-handling guard: 'result = run_pipeline(list(tickers), copy)' followed by 'if inspect.isawaitable(result): result = await result'. This satisfies both async and sync stubs without changing the run_pipeline call shape."}, {"file": "tests/test_wiring.py", "line": 1, "issue": "Acceptance gate not met: the suite is at 111 passed / 2 failed / 0 skipped versus the required 113/113 with zero failures and zero skips (passed > baseline is insufficient; the reviewer gate rejects any failing test).", "remediation": "Apply the two coroutine-handling fixes above, re-run the full pytest suite (tests/test_wiring.py, tests/test_smoke.py, tests/test_cli.py included), and confirm 113 passed / 0 failed / 0 skipped before resubmitting."}]}
