{"ts": "2026-09-04T23:34:26Z", "task_id": "TASK-7013", "attempt": 1, "verdict": "CHANGES_REQUESTED", "failed_tests": 6, "real_execution": true, "applied_files": 2, "feedback": [{"file": "src/cli.py", "line": 117, "issue": "Six tests/test_wiring.py tests fail with 'AttributeError: module src.cli has no attribute _store' (pinned at tests/test_wiring.py:259). The full-file rewrite dropped the module-level _store DecisionStore that the pre-seeded tests patch/inspect; _run_and_print constructs a local DecisionStore instead, so injected fakes never receive log_decision calls and monkeypatch.setattr raises.", "remediation": "Restore a module-level store in src/cli.py, e.g. `_store = DecisionStore(db_path=os.environ.get('DECISIONS_DB', 'data/decisions.sqlite3'))` (keep construction exception-safe or lazily initialized if import-time DB creation is a concern, but the attribute `src.cli._store` must exist), and have _run_and_print call `_store.log_decision(_jsonable(decision))` via the module-level name at call time so monkeypatched fakes receive the calls; keep the per-decision try/except with a single warning line."}, {"file": "src/cli.py", "line": 141, "issue": "The decisions command constructs its own local DecisionStore instead of reading through the module-level _store, duplicating the db_path literal and ignoring any store the tests inject.", "remediation": "Use the module-level `_store.get_recent_decisions(limit=10)` in the decisions command so both the audit-write and audit-read paths share one patchable store."}, {"file": "src/cli.py", "line": 68, "issue": "The fetch_ohlcv closure returns `data['Close']` directly; under yfinance MultiIndex columns that selection is itself a DataFrame, violating the pinned contract that the closure always returns a pd.Series (take the first column of the Close selection when it is a DataFrame).", "remediation": "After selecting Close (or the first column when 'Close' is absent), coerce the result: `close = data['Close']; if isinstanc